From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 08:55:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 486/488] [DS4.1] SP and rank-order pad rows: zeros from
 TileLang's fill

721317853 dropped the torch zero fills of prefill SP's pad rows and left
them arbitrary. They reach no real row, but uninitialized values (NaN among
them) would still be normalized, routed and sent to experts, and the work
they cause would change from run to run. The pad rows are zeroed again, by
TileLang's 16-byte fill (columns.zero_), declared with the collectives, so
no torch fill returns. The tests require the zeros and refuse torch's fill.
